                <pb facs="0815" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/232: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-31T12:00:00-05:00">December 31,
                        1929—noon</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>435. Your 1200, December 29, 2 p.m., and 1204, December 30, 5 p.m. For your
                    instruction and the guidance of American officials in China, the Department does
                    not regard the declaration of the Chinese Government as having altered the legal
                        <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi>. You may so inform your
                    colleagues.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
